{"event":"step_update","step_update":{"conversation_id":"0f8ec410-73a3-4005-b0a0-8e77165078bb","step_index":64,"state":"DONE","step_type":"tool","tool_name":"run_command","duration_seconds":0.08917,"tool_info":{"name":"run_command","parameters":{"CommandLine":"git log -p -n 3"},"output":"Command exited with code 0.\n\nCommand output:\ncommit b5045374f32c072b4b6aa12418ad1a0a17df0c98 (HEAD -\u003e main)\r\nAuthor: dev \u003cdev@local\u003e\r\nDate:   Mon Nov 9 15:06:48 2026 -0300\r\n\r\n    base\r\n\r\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000..0699eae\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/README.md\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@\r\n+# headless Vibe runs (my setup)\r\n+\r\n+I run Mistral Vibe CLI 3.1.0 headless on Devstral 2 through OpenRouter, for batch coding tasks. Each run goes\r\n+through `run-vibe.sh`, which starts Vibe inside a macOS sandbox (`agent.sb`) with an empty scratch HOME and an\r\n+allowlisted environment, because the agent has a real shell and everything it sees goes to OpenRouter.\r\n+\r\n+- `run-vibe.sh \"\u003cprompt\u003e\" [workdir]`: one run; `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` comes from my shell (it is set, and it works\r\n+  with curl against OpenRouter).\r\n+- `agent.sb`: the sandbox. It must keep the agent away from my home folder and the Keychain; that is the whole point.\r\n+- `vibe/config.toml`: the Vibe config (OpenRouter provider, Devstral 2).\r\n+- `logs/last-run.out`, `logs/last-run.err`: the last run (`./run-vibe.sh \"say hi\" /tmp/x`, printed `exit 2`).\r\n+\r\n+Every run ends within a second or two with exit 2 and does nothing; no export folder is written.\r\ndiff --git a/agent.sb b/agent.sb\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000..b94988f\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/agent.sb\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@\r\n+;; macOS sandbox for the headless agent: it has a real shell and everything it prints goes to OpenRouter and the\r\n+;; model host, so my real home (and the Keychain) must stay unreachable. The only things read from the home are\r\n+;; Vibe's own install (pipx venv and its launcher). Network stays open. HOME is passed with -D.\r\n+(version 1)\r\n+(allow default)\r\n+(deny file-read-data (subpath (param \"HOME\")))\r\n+(deny file-write* (subpath (param \"HOME\")))\r\n+(allow file-read-data (subpath (string-append (param \"HOME\") \"/.local/pipx\")))\r\n+(allow file-read-data (literal (string-append (param \"HOME\") \"/.local/bin/vibe\")))\r\n+(deny process-exec (literal \"/bin/launchctl\") (literal \"/usr/bin/security\") (literal \"/usr/bin/osascript\"))\r\ndiff --git a/logs/last-run.err b/logs/last-run.err\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000..cd6d9ad\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/logs/last-run.err\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@\r\n+Reading API keys from the macOS Keychain (set them as environment variables to skip this)\r\n+Error: [Errno 1] Operation not permitted: '/usr/bin/security'\r\ndiff --git a/logs/last-run.out b/logs/last-run.out\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000..e69de29\r\ndiff --git a/run-vibe.sh b/run-vibe.sh\r\nnew file mode 100755\r\nindex 0000000..c4a5223\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/run-vibe.sh\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@\r\n+#!/usr/bin/env bash\r\n+# run-vibe.sh \"\u003cprompt\u003e\" [workdir]: one headless Mistral Vibe run on Devstral 2 through OpenRouter, inside agent.sb.\r\n+# The agent gets an empty scratch HOME and VIBE_HOME and only the environment names listed below (env -i), so none of\r\n+# my other secrets reach it. OPENROUTER_API_KEY must be set in the calling shell.\r\n+set -u\r\n+D=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" \u0026\u0026 pwd)\"\r\n+PROMPT=$1; W=${2:-$PWD}\r\n+REAL=\"$HOME\"\r\n+VIBE=\"${VIBE:-$REAL/.local/bin/vibe}\"\r\n+[ -n \"${OPENROUTER_API_KEY:-}\" ] || { echo \"set OPENROUTER_API_KEY first\"; exit 1; }\r\n+SH=$(mktemp -d /tmp/vhome-XXXXXX); VH=$(mktemp -d /tmp/vibehome-XXXXXX)\r\n+cp \"$D/vibe/config.toml\" \"$VH/config.toml\"\r\n+mkdir -p \"$D/logs\"\r\n+( cd \"$W\" \u0026\u0026 env -i PATH=\"$PATH\" TERM=\"${TERM:-dumb}\" LANG=\"${LANG:-en_US.UTF-8}\" HOME=\"$SH\" VIBE_HOME=\"$VH\" \\\r\n+    OPENROUTER_API_KEY=\"$OPENROUTER_API_KEY\" \\\r\n+    sandbox-exec -D HOME=\"$REAL\" -f \"$D/agent.sb\" \\\r\n+    \"$VIBE\" -p \"$PROMPT\" --model devstral --auto-approve --trust --output streaming --output-dir \"$VH/out\" \\\r\n+      --max-price 1.5 --time-limit 1200 \u003c /dev/null \u003e \"$D/logs/last-run.out\" 2\u003e \"$D/logs/last-run.err\" )\r\n+rc=$?\r\n+[ -d \"$VH/out\" ] \u0026\u0026 cp -R \"$VH/out\" \"$D/logs/last-run-export\"\r\n+chmod -R u+w \"$SH\" \"$VH\" 2\u003e/dev/null; rm -rf \"$SH\" \"$VH\"\r\n+echo \"exit $rc\"; exit $rc\r\ndiff --git a/vibe/config.toml b/vibe/config.toml\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000..4a44d67\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/vibe/config.toml\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@\r\n+# Vibe config for the headless runs: Devstral 2 (mistralai/devstral-2512) through OpenRouter, in Mistral's own\r\n+# agent, Vibe CLI 3.1.0. Everything that would talk to Mistral's own services is off (telemetry, updates, connectors).\r\n+active_model = \"devstral\"\r\n+enable_telemetry = false\r\n+enable_update_checks = false\r\n+enable_auto_update = false\r\n+enable_notifications = false\r\n+enable_connectors = false\r\n+enable_mcp = false\r\n+show_greeting = false\r\n+outside_workdir = \"deny\"\r\n+\r\n+[[providers]]\r\n+name = \"openrouter\"\r\n+api_base = \"https://openrouter.ai/api/v1\"\r\n+api_key_env_var = \"OPENROUTER_API_KEY\"\r\n+api_style = \"openai\"\r\n+backend = \"generic\"\r\n+\r\n+[models.devstral]\r\n+name = \"mistralai/devstral-2512\"\r\n+provider = \"openrouter\"\r\n+alias = \"devstral\"\r\n+temperature = 0.2\r\n+input_price = 0.4\r\n+output_price = 2.0\r\n+max_context_length = 262144\r\n"}}}
