{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"0f8ec410-73a3-4005-b0a0-8e77165078bb","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Cause and Fix Summary\n\n#### Why it failed:\nDuring startup, Mistral Vibe attempts to resolve default credentials (including looking for `MISTRAL_API_KEY`). If the key is not found in the environment, it queries the macOS Keychain by attempting to execute `/usr/bin/security`. However, [agent.sb](file:///tmp/h-FGcl0r/agent.sb#L10) explicitly denies process execution of `/usr/bin/security`:\n```scheme\n(deny process-exec (literal \"/bin/launchctl\") (literal \"/usr/bin/security\") (literal \"/usr/bin/osascript\"))\n```\nBecause [run-vibe.sh](file:///tmp/h-FGcl0r/run-vibe.sh) cleared the environment with `env -i`, Vibe attempted to call `/usr/bin/security`, which macOS rejected with `[Errno 1] Operation not permitted: '/usr/bin/security'`, crashing the process immediately with exit code 2.\n\n#### Fix:\nVibe supports `VIBE_TEST_DISABLE_KEYRING=1` to disable OS keyring/Keychain access entirely. We updated the `env -i` invocation in [run-vibe.sh](file:///tmp/h-FGcl0r/run-vibe.sh#L14-L18) to include `VIBE_TEST_DISABLE_KEYRING=\"1\"`.\n\nThe detailed analysis and resolution have been documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-FGcl0r/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":826.022361,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":575001,"output_tokens":20305,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":10045393,"total_tokens":595306}}}
